---@class posthog.autoresearch.CreateAutoresearchTrainingRunsCompleteRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field pipeline_id string
---@field id string A UUID string identifying this autoresearch training run.
---@field best_iteration_id? string|distilled.Null Advisory nomination. The server promotes the kept iteration with the highest holdout_score; this id only breaks a tie at that score, and a lower-scoring nomination is logged and ignored.
---@field model_explanation? posthog.autoresearch.ModelExplanationField Global feature importance / directionality bundle for the champion model card.
---@field recommended_next? string What a future run should try next, given what this run learned. Stored in the run summary so the next run reads it during orientation. Keep it short and concrete; max 2000 characters.
---@field distillation? string A 1–2 sentence distillation of what this run learned — the winning signal, the key transform, the dead-ends. Stored in the run summary as the cheapest thing the next run reads. Max 2000 characters.
---@field reader_summary? string|distilled.Null One or two plain sentences for people on what this run learned. Max 600 characters.
---@field headline? string|distilled.Null A short title for people, at most 60 characters, on what this run learned. Use plain words, with no column names, SQL or model jargon. Longer text is cut, not rejected.
---@field next_steps? posthog.autoresearch.CreateAutoresearchTrainingRunsCompleteRequestNextStepsList|distilled.Null Short next steps for people, at most 5 items of a few words each (max 80 characters per item).
---@field report_notebook_short_id? string Short id of the report notebook you built for this run. Stored in the run summary only if the notebook exists in this project; an unknown id is dropped and does not fail the completion.

---Short next steps for people, at most 5 items of a few words each (max 80 characters per item).
