---@class posthog.autoresearch.OnlinePerformance
---@field rows posthog.autoresearch.OnlinePerformanceRowsList One row per model per validated prediction date, newest date first. Empty until a prediction horizon has elapsed and online validation has run.
---@field segment_thresholds posthog.autoresearch.PredictionSegmentThresholds The current cut points between the Likely, Possible and Unlikely segments, set by lift over the realized base rate. They do not depend on limit.

---@class posthog.autoresearch.OnlinePerformanceRow
---@field validation_run_id string UUID of the validation run that recorded these metrics.
---@field prediction_date string Date the predictions were made for (UTC).
---@field horizon_days number Prediction horizon, in days, the predictions were made under.
---@field weekday number ISO weekday of the prediction date: 1 is Monday and 7 is Sunday. Use it to find weekday effects.
---@field model_id string UUID of the model that emitted the predictions.
---@field emitted_role string Role the model had when it emitted the predictions: 'champion' or 'challenger'.
---@field current_role string Role the model has now: 'champion', 'challenger', 'archived', or 'deleted'. A former champion that a promotion archived keeps its rows.
---@field n_scored number Number of users the model scored on this date.
---@field n_positive number Number of scored users who did the target event in the horizon.
---@field base_rate number Fraction of scored users who did the target event (n_positive / n_scored).
---@field mean_p_y number|distilled.Null Mean predicted probability. Compare it with base_rate: a higher value means the model over-predicts. Null for dates validated before this metric existed.
---@field realized_auc number|distilled.Null Realized ROC AUC against actual outcomes. Null when the date has one class only.
---@field realized_auc_ci_low number|distilled.Null Lower bound of the 95% AUC interval (Hanley-McNeil). Null when realized_auc is null.
---@field realized_auc_ci_high number|distilled.Null Upper bound of the 95% AUC interval (Hanley-McNeil). Null when realized_auc is null.
---@field brier_score number|distilled.Null Brier score. Lower is better.
---@field calibration_error number|distilled.Null Expected calibration error over 10 equal-width bins. Lower is better.
---@field lift_at_10 number|distilled.Null Positives in the top 10% by score, relative to a random 10%.
---@field lift_at_20 number|distilled.Null Positives in the top 20% by score, relative to a random 20%.
---@field average_precision number|distilled.Null Average precision: area under the precision-recall curve. Higher is better, and a random model scores about base_rate. Null when no scored user did the target event, or for dates validated before this metric existed.
---@field confusion posthog.autoresearch.ConfusionByCutoff|distilled.Null Confusion counts, precision and recall at three cutoffs: top 10%, top 20%, and the Likely segment. Null for dates validated before this metric existed.
---@field likely_threshold number|distilled.Null The Likely cut point the 'likely' confusion counts used for this date, from the base rate of the dates checked before it. Null when confusion is null.
---@field calibration_bins posthog.autoresearch.OnlinePerformanceRowCalibrationBinsList|distilled.Null Calibration table with up to 10 bins cut at score quantiles, lowest scores first. Users with equal scores share a bin, so heavy ties give fewer bins. Null for dates validated before this metric existed.
---@field warning string|distilled.Null 'single_class_no_auc' when every scored user had the same outcome, otherwise null.
---@field validated_at string|distilled.Null When the validation run completed.

---Calibration table with up to 10 bins cut at score quantiles, lowest scores first. Users with equal scores share a bin, so heavy ties give fewer bins. Null for dates validated before this metric existed.
