---@class posthog.autoresearch.PredictionSegmentThresholds
---@field likely_threshold number Users with a score at or above this probability are in the Likely segment: likely_lift times the base rate, capped halfway between the base rate and 1. A fixed cut point when base_rate_source is fixed.
---@field possible_threshold number Users with a score at or above this probability and below likely_threshold are in the Possible segment, and users below it are Unlikely. Equal to base_rate, or a fixed cut point when base_rate_source is fixed.
---@field likely_lift number How many times the base rate a score must reach to be in the Likely segment.
---@field base_rate number|distilled.Null The base rate the cut points use. When base_rate_source is realized, the fraction of the champion's scored users who did the target event, pooled over the newest checked dates. When base_rate_source is training, the fraction of the champion's training population that did it. Null when base_rate_source is fixed.
---@field base_rate_dates number Number of checked prediction dates the base rate pools.
---@field base_rate_source posthog.autoresearch.BaseRateSourceEnum Where the cut points come from. realized: the checked dates hold enough positives. training: no realized base rate yet, so the champion's training population sets it. fixed: neither is available, so fixed cut points apply. * `realized` - Realized * `training` - Training * `fixed` - Fixed
---@field champion_mean_p_y number|distilled.Null The current champion's mean predicted probability over the checked dates it scored as champion. Null until those dates hold enough positives.
---@field champion_base_rate number|distilled.Null The real rate of the target event over the same dates as champion_mean_p_y.
---@field scores_miscalibrated boolean True when champion_mean_p_y is far above or below champion_base_rate. The scores are then not probabilities (for example after class weighting in train.py), so a score of likely_lift times the base rate does not mean the user is that many times as likely to convert.

---@class posthog.autoresearch.ProjectLimits
---@field max_training_runs_per_day number Sandbox training runs the project may start in any 24 hours, across all its pipelines. 0 means training is turned off.
---@field training_runs_used number Sandbox training runs the project started in the last 24 hours, across all its pipelines.
---@field next_slot_at string|distilled.Null When the next training run can start, while the project is at its daily limit. Null while a run can start now, and when training is turned off.
---@field max_iterations_per_run number Most experiments any one training run gets. A pipeline's iterations_per_run above this is lowered to it.
---@field max_live_pipelines number Most pipelines the project may have live (bootstrapping, running or converged, or a draft with an open training run, which goes live when the run promotes). Starting a draft's first training run or resuming a paused pipeline is refused at this limit.
---@field live_pipelines number Pipelines that count against max_live_pipelines now. Can exceed it if the limit was lowered.

---* `kept` - kept
---* `discarded` - discarded
---* `crashed` - crashed
---@alias posthog.autoresearch.RecordIterationStatusEnum "kept"|"discarded"|"crashed"

