---@class posthog.autoresearch.UpdateAutoresearchPartialRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field id string A UUID string identifying this autoresearch pipeline.
---@field name? string Display name for the pipeline.
---@field description? string Optional free-text description.
---@field target_event? string PostHog event name to predict, e.g. '$pageview' or 'signed_up'. Omit when predicting an action target (pass target_definition instead).
---@field target_definition? posthog.autoresearch.UpdateAutoresearchPartialRequestTargetDefinition Omit (or pass {"type": "event"}) to predict target_event; pass {"type": "action", "action_id": N} to predict a PostHog action. No other shapes are accepted.
---@field horizon_days? number Prediction horizon in days (1-365). The model predicts whether the target event occurs within this window.
---@field training_lookback_days? number How far back to look for training examples (7-730 days). Larger windows give more data but may include stale behavior. Default: 180.
---@field training_population? any Training population filter. Use {} for all identified users.
---@field inference_population? any Inference population filter. Defaults to training_population if not set.
---@field cadence_days? number Re-score the inference population every N days (1-365). Default: 1.
---@field iteration_budget? number Deprecated: scheduled training no longer reads it. Use iterations_per_run.
---@field iterations_per_run? number Experiments the agent may try in each training run (1-50). Each experiment costs agent time and queries, so a higher value costs more per run. Scheduled runs and Train now use it. Default: 5.
---@field research_interval_days? posthog.autoresearch.ResearchIntervalDaysEnum|number|distilled.Null Days between scheduled research runs once the first burst of daily runs ends: 7, 14, 30, 60 or 90. Null means only when asked: no scheduled research, so the only training cost comes from runs you start and from rescue runs for a model that cannot score. A shorter interval costs more. Default: 7. * `7` - 7 * `14` - 14 * `30` - 30 * `60` - 60 * `90` - 90
---@field agent_model? string|distilled.Null Model the training agent runs on, a model id from the PostHog Tasks catalogue such as 'claude-opus-5-5', 'claude-sonnet-5-5' or 'gpt-6.1-sol'. Null or omitted uses the autoresearch default, Claude Opus 5.5. A larger model costs more per training run. Scheduled runs and Train now use it.
---@field agent_reasoning_effort? string|distilled.Null Reasoning effort for the training agent, such as 'low', 'medium' or 'high'. It must be one the model supports, and without agent_model it is checked against the default model. Null or omitted uses the autoresearch default, medium. Higher effort costs more per training run.
---@field success_auc? number|distilled.Null Target AUC threshold (0-1). Training stops early if reached. Default: 0.75.
---@field plateau_iterations? number Stop training if no improvement in this many consecutive iterations (at least 1). Default: 10.
---@field output_person_property? string Person property name for the prediction score, e.g. 'predicted_p_pageview'. Auto-derived from target_event if omitted. Letters, digits, and _ $ . - only, and it cannot start with $ (reserved for PostHog's own properties); must be unique among this project's non-archived pipelines.
---@field write_person_property? boolean Write the champion's score to output_person_property on each scored person at every live scoring run. Default: false. Needed to target people by score in feature flags, cohorts, workflows and insights. Prediction events, validation and segments work without it. Turning it off, or archiving or deleting the pipeline while it is on, removes the property from the people it scored.

