---@class posthog.autoresearch.ValidatePipelineResponse
---@field can_proceed boolean False when any warning has severity 'error'. Creation does not enforce it, but a definition with an 'error' 'population_too_large' or 'horizon_exceeds_lookback' cannot train.
---@field requires_acknowledgement boolean True if there are non-blocking warnings the user should acknowledge before proceeding.
---@field estimated_training_rows number|distilled.Null Estimated number of user-level training rows based on the population and lookback window.
---@field positive_count number|distilled.Null Estimated number of positive examples (users who performed the target event).
---@field negative_count number|distilled.Null Estimated number of negative examples.
---@field base_rate number|distilled.Null Fraction of the training population that performed the target event.
---@field inference_population_size number|distilled.Null Estimated number of users in the inference (daily scoring) population.
---@field warnings posthog.autoresearch.ValidatePipelineResponseWarningsList List of validation warnings. Check 'severity' and 'code'.
---@field error string|distilled.Null Why validation did not run, or null when it did. A query error in the definition itself is passed through; any other failure is a generic message and the detail is logged.

---List of validation warnings. Check 'severity' and 'code'.
---@alias posthog.autoresearch.ValidatePipelineResponseWarningsList posthog.autoresearch.ValidationWarning[]

---@class posthog.autoresearch.ValidationWarning
---@field code string Machine-readable warning code. 'horizon_exceeds_lookback', and 'population_too_large' with severity 'error', mean a run would fail: fix the definition before creating. 'population_too_large' with severity 'info' means training uses a sample of the population, or each scoring run scores a rolling part of it: users never scored first, then users whose last score was oldest. 'low_volume', 'low_positives' and 'low_negatives' mean the data is too thin for a reliable model (severity 'error', advisory). 'moderate_volume', 'mostly_anonymous_population', 'extreme_imbalance' and 'near_universal' are severity 'warning'.
---@field message string Human-readable warning description.
---@field severity posthog.autoresearch.ValidationWarningSeverityEnum Severity level. 'error' means training would fail or the data is too thin for a reliable model; see 'code' for which. 'warning' is worth acknowledging. Creation enforces none of them. * `info` - info * `warning` - warning * `error` - error

---* `info` - info
---* `warning` - warning
---* `error` - error
---@alias posthog.autoresearch.ValidationWarningSeverityEnum "info"|"warning"|"error"

---* `pending` - Pending
---* `running` - Running
---* `completed` - Completed
---* `failed` - Failed
---@alias posthog.autoresearch.ZendeskImportJobStatusEnum "pending"|"running"|"completed"|"failed"

